<section class="sec" id="how"><div class="wrap"><div class="intro rv"><h2 class="h2">We give you the AI. You bring the judgment.</h2><p class="lede">Run it like a fund: pick your analysts, hear their pitches, and weigh every idea from both sides.</p></div></div><div class="fcar rv"><div class="fcar-track"><article class="fcard"><div class="ftext"><h3>Good judgment is small data</h3><p>Investing has no right answer for AI to find: ask a model what a stock is worth and you get the consensus, which is already in the price. To paraphrase Galileo, reasoning is like racing, not hauling: one thoroughbred outruns a hundred farm horses.</p></div><div class="appwin"><div class="ph shot"><span>Placeholder</span><small>Good judgment is small data</small></div></div></article><article class="fcard"><div class="ftext"><h3>Pick your analysts</h3><p>Olives reward reasoning that holds up, not luck or hype, and they’re earned asset by asset. Use them as a starting point, then build your bench using your own judgment.</p></div><div class="appwin"><div class="ph shot"><span>Placeholder</span><small>Leaderboard and analysts’ Olives</small></div></div></article><article class="fcard"><div class="ftext"><h3>Chair your investment committee</h3><p>Your analysts pitch you their best ideas, with the reasoning behind them, and alert you when they rethink a Value. You make the call.</p></div><div class="appwin"><div class="ph shot"><span>Placeholder</span><small>Ideas pitched by your analysts</small></div></div></article><article class="fcard"><div class="ftext"><h3>John Maven AI, at your service</h3><p>He covers every asset no analyst has claimed yet. Ask him where analysts stand on an asset, or what’s being said about it on X.</p></div><div class="appwin"><div class="ph shot"><span>Placeholder</span><small>John Maven AI</small></div></div></article></div>
